WEBVTT

00:04:28.458 --> 00:04:31.672
Well, it's like a vast, cavernous expanse,

00:04:31.696 --> 00:04:33.760
where there are people
talking about sports,

00:04:33.784 --> 00:04:36.465
arguing about politics,
yelling at each other, flirting,

00:04:36.489 --> 00:04:37.659
trying to get a job,

00:04:37.683 --> 00:04:40.426
all in the same place,
with no walls, no divisions,

00:04:40.450 --> 00:04:43.299
and the owner gets paid more
the louder the noise is.

00:04:43.323 --> 00:04:44.363
(Laughter)

00:04:44.387 --> 00:04:45.854
No wonder it's a mess.

00:04:46.744 --> 00:04:49.379
And this raises another thing
that become obvious

00:04:49.403 --> 00:04:52.269
when we think about platforms
in terms of physical space.

00:04:52.997 --> 00:04:56.132
Good physical spaces
are almost always structured.

00:04:56.640 --> 00:04:57.790
They have rules.

00:04:59.108 --> 00:05:05.729
Silicon Valley is built on this idea
that unstructured space is conducive